1
00:00:02,467 --> 00:00:04,219
KATARA: Water.

2
00:00:04,886 --> 00:00:06,471
Earth.

3
00:00:06,763 --> 00:00:08,681
Fire.

4
00:00:09,015 --> 00:00:10,683
Air.

5
00:00:11,059 --> 00:00:14,521
Long ago the four nations
lived together in harmony.

6
00:00:14,729 --> 00:00:18,900
Then everything changed
when the Fire Nation attacked.

7
00:00:19,484 --> 00:00:23,363
Only the Avatar, master of all
four elements, could stop them.

8
00:00:23,571 --> 00:00:25,532
But when the world needed him most

9
00:00:25,615 --> 00:00:26,950
He vanished.

10
00:00:27,367 --> 00:00:30,912
100 years passed and my brother and I
discovered the new Avatar,

11
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:32,747
an airbender named Aang.

12
00:00:33,122 --> 00:00:35,041
And although his airbending skills
are great,

13
00:00:35,166 --> 00:00:37,752
he has a lot to learn before
he's ready to save anyone.

14
00:00:37,961 --> 00:00:38,962
AANG: Oof.

15
00:00:39,045 --> 00:00:42,298
But I believe Aang can save the world.

16
00:00:42,590 --> 00:00:44,342
[ ♪... ]

17
00:00:47,845 --> 00:00:50,223
( MAN READING )

18
00:00:50,431 --> 00:00:54,018
Ever since you joined us, you've been
nothing but selfish and unhelpful.

19
00:00:54,102 --> 00:00:55,103
What?

20
00:00:55,311 --> 00:00:57,105
Look here, sugar queen.

21
00:00:57,188 --> 00:01:00,942
I gave up everything I had so that
I could teach Aang earthbending.

22
00:01:01,025 --> 00:01:04,153
So don't you talk to me
about being selfish.

23
00:01:04,362 --> 00:01:06,322
The Avatar is alive.

24
00:01:06,614 --> 00:01:09,117
I want you to find him, and end him.

25
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:12,370
SOKKA: This is crazy!

26
00:01:12,579 --> 00:01:14,998
How can we beat a guy
who blows things up with his mind?

27
00:01:15,206 --> 00:01:16,249
AANG: We can't!

28
00:01:31,431 --> 00:01:33,516
( PANTING )

29
00:01:33,725 --> 00:01:36,769
( GRUNTING )

30
00:01:36,978 --> 00:01:38,354
How could you do this to me?

31
00:01:38,563 --> 00:01:40,023
You betrayed me.

32
00:01:41,190 --> 00:01:42,734
You brought this on yourself.

33
00:01:43,318 --> 00:01:44,402
I had no choice.

34
00:02:05,381 --> 00:02:07,592
Okay, I'm ready for some training.

35
00:02:26,194 --> 00:02:27,695
Good job, Twinkle-toes.

36
00:02:27,779 --> 00:02:29,364
Visualize, then attack.

37
00:02:30,948 --> 00:02:32,283
( GROANS )

38
00:02:33,117 --> 00:02:35,370
Maybe you should take
your own advice, Toph.

39
00:02:36,245 --> 00:02:37,246
TOPH: What's the matter?

40
00:02:37,330 --> 00:02:39,457
Can't handle some dirt,
Madam Fussy-britches?

41
00:02:44,629 --> 00:02:47,674
Oh, sorry, did I splash you, mud slug?

42
00:02:52,387 --> 00:02:54,097
( BOTH GRUNTING )

43
00:02:54,806 --> 00:02:56,349
Are we taking a break?

44
00:02:58,351 --> 00:02:59,519
( SCREAMING )

45
00:02:59,727 --> 00:03:00,770
Sneak attack!

46
00:03:00,853 --> 00:03:01,979
( GRUNTS )

47
00:03:02,689 --> 00:03:05,316
Sokka, sneak attacks don't work
if you yell it out loud.

48
00:03:07,110 --> 00:03:08,945
( GRUNTING )

49
00:03:09,237 --> 00:03:10,279
Hungry for a mud pie?

50
00:03:10,530 --> 00:03:12,115
( SPUTTERS )

51
00:03:12,740 --> 00:03:15,243
I'll give you a mud pie.

52
00:03:15,868 --> 00:03:18,746
( GRUNTING )

53
00:03:20,832 --> 00:03:23,376
Uh, guys, I thought we were
supposed to be training me.

54
00:03:24,961 --> 00:03:26,963
Very well, pupil.

55
00:03:27,130 --> 00:03:29,424
I believe we've had enough training
for today.

56
00:03:30,258 --> 00:03:33,886
While Katara cleans up,
let's go have some fun.

57
00:03:34,262 --> 00:03:36,097
- Yes!
- Yeah!

58
00:03:37,765 --> 00:03:39,976
( BIRDS SCREECHING )

59
00:03:46,441 --> 00:03:48,776
SOKKA: Look at all those messenger hawks.

60
00:03:48,985 --> 00:03:51,571
You know, I've been thinking
about getting one for myself.

61
00:03:51,654 --> 00:03:53,448
That way, I wouldn't
have to talk to anyone.

62
00:03:53,573 --> 00:03:55,283
I could just send them messages.

63
00:03:55,616 --> 00:03:58,786
I got to say, I like the idea
of not talking to you.

64
00:03:59,495 --> 00:04:02,373
So, guys, what are we gonna get
with our last silver piece?

65
00:04:03,499 --> 00:04:05,001
We can get more money.

66
00:04:06,419 --> 00:04:07,545
Right there.

67
00:04:16,179 --> 00:04:18,890
TOPH: This is where you seeing people
are at a disadvantage.

68
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:22,602
Everyone guesses wrong because the dealer
moves the rock at the last minute.

69
00:04:23,019 --> 00:04:25,021
But, I can feel it with my earthbending.

70
00:04:30,067 --> 00:04:31,152
( GASPS )

71
00:04:31,402 --> 00:04:32,737
( CRYING )

72
00:04:38,785 --> 00:04:41,913
You there. Want to play a friendly game?

73
00:04:41,996 --> 00:04:43,581
How could I possibly play?

74
00:04:43,998 --> 00:04:45,416
I'm blind.

75
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:47,502
You don't have to see to be lucky.

76
00:05:13,736 --> 00:05:14,737
"Flamey-o," Toph.

77
00:05:15,029 --> 00:05:16,906
DEALER: Wow, fancy guessing.

78
00:05:17,114 --> 00:05:19,033
You are amazing at this.

79
00:05:19,325 --> 00:05:21,994
Would you like to make the game
a little more interesting?

80
00:05:22,495 --> 00:05:23,704
More interesting?

81
00:05:24,121 --> 00:05:25,248
How?

82
00:05:25,373 --> 00:05:29,627
Well, let's say you toss in
your friend's fine sword there.

83
00:05:29,710 --> 00:05:34,090
Then I'll put up 20 silver pieces
against it, and that's more interesting.

84
00:05:35,216 --> 00:05:37,134
I'll do it for 40 silver pieces.

85
00:05:37,301 --> 00:05:38,302
( EXCLAIMS )

86
00:05:38,553 --> 00:05:40,596
Forty silver pieces it is.

87
00:06:02,201 --> 00:06:04,537
Sorry, little lady, but...

88
00:06:04,620 --> 00:06:05,663
Huh?

89
00:06:05,830 --> 00:06:06,873
I won!

90
00:06:10,877 --> 00:06:13,462
( LAUGHING )

91
00:06:16,883 --> 00:06:20,261
Where did you guys get
the money to buy all this stuff?

92
00:06:20,344 --> 00:06:21,554
Toph got us money.

93
00:06:22,054 --> 00:06:25,892
She scammed one of those guys in town
who moves shells around all sneaky-like.

94
00:06:27,018 --> 00:06:28,895
She used earthbending to win the game.

95
00:06:28,978 --> 00:06:29,979
Classic.

96
00:06:30,062 --> 00:06:31,606
Ah, so she cheated.

97
00:06:32,231 --> 00:06:34,567
Hey, I only cheated
because he was cheating.

98
00:06:34,775 --> 00:06:36,027
I cheated a cheater.

99
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:37,486
What's wrong with that?

100
00:06:37,862 --> 00:06:40,656
I'm just saying, this isn't something
we should make a habit of doing.

101
00:06:41,073 --> 00:06:44,201
Why? Because it's fun, and you hate fun?

102
00:06:44,577 --> 00:06:46,287
I don't hate fun.

103
00:06:46,662 --> 00:06:48,706
See? Fun.

104
00:06:50,750 --> 00:06:52,376
( CHATTERS )

105
00:06:52,668 --> 00:06:55,046
Katara, I'll personally make you
an Avatar-promise

106
00:06:55,129 --> 00:06:57,214
that we won't make a habit
of doing these scams.

107
00:07:45,304 --> 00:07:46,305
( STOMPS )

108
00:07:47,139 --> 00:07:48,140
( BELL RINGS )

109
00:08:24,802 --> 00:08:27,471
Guys, I think these scams
have gone far enough.

110
00:08:27,555 --> 00:08:29,849
If you keep doing them,
something bad is gonna happen.

111
00:08:29,932 --> 00:08:33,728
Could you for once stop being
such a sourpuss and just lighten up?

112
00:08:34,270 --> 00:08:35,521
Oh, I'm sorry.

113
00:08:35,604 --> 00:08:37,314
You think I should be more like you?

114
00:08:37,523 --> 00:08:39,025
Like some wild child?

115
00:08:39,358 --> 00:08:40,818
Yeah, maybe.

116
00:08:41,027 --> 00:08:42,862
Maybe then,
you'd see how great we have it.

117
00:08:42,945 --> 00:08:44,113
I mean, look at us.

118
00:08:44,196 --> 00:08:46,574
We're traveling around the world,
making easy money,

119
00:08:46,657 --> 00:08:49,493
having fun, with no parents
to tell us what to do.

120
00:08:50,369 --> 00:08:52,246
Ah, I see...

121
00:08:52,329 --> 00:08:54,331
You're acting like this
because of your parents.

122
00:08:54,999 --> 00:08:57,084
- Whatever.
- They were controlling over you,

123
00:08:57,168 --> 00:09:00,296
so you ran away, and now you act
like your parents don't exist.

124
00:09:00,546 --> 00:09:03,174
You act like you hate them, but you don't.

125
00:09:03,424 --> 00:09:04,675
You just feel guilty.

126
00:09:04,884 --> 00:09:06,010
I do hate them.

127
00:09:06,260 --> 00:09:07,344
I don't think so.

128
00:09:07,678 --> 00:09:09,096
I think you miss them.

129
00:09:09,263 --> 00:09:13,726
But you just don't wanna deal with that,
so instead you act like this crazy person.

130
00:09:13,934 --> 00:09:16,353
Look, I ran away to help Aang.

131
00:09:16,604 --> 00:09:18,272
You know what? It doesn't matter.

132
00:09:18,355 --> 00:09:20,941
These scams put us all at risk,
and we don't need that.

133
00:09:21,108 --> 00:09:23,194
We've already got some
third-eyed freak after us.

134
00:09:23,694 --> 00:09:25,362
Speaking of that third-eyed freak

135
00:09:25,571 --> 00:09:27,448
I think I've come up with a name for him.

136
00:09:27,531 --> 00:09:30,993
What do you think of
"Sparky-sparky Boom Man"?

137
00:09:31,702 --> 00:09:33,079
Just think about it.

138
00:09:33,370 --> 00:09:35,748
We have enough money.
You need to stop this.

139
00:09:36,332 --> 00:09:39,293
I'll stop when I want to stop,
and not when you tell me.

140
00:09:46,759 --> 00:09:48,677
MOMO: ( CHATTERS )

141
00:09:48,844 --> 00:09:50,763
Speaking of money, I'm off to spend some.

142
00:09:51,305 --> 00:09:52,473
See you guys later.

143
00:09:58,521 --> 00:10:00,564
Hawky, welcome to team Avatar.

144
00:10:01,190 --> 00:10:03,109
My name's Sokka, and I'm your new owner,

145
00:10:03,192 --> 00:10:06,570
and as such, I should warn you that
there's already a lemur in our group,

146
00:10:06,654 --> 00:10:08,948
so I don't want to see any fighting.

147
00:10:09,031 --> 00:10:10,074
( SQUAWKS )

148
00:10:10,324 --> 00:10:11,659
( COOING )
Good wittle messenger hawky.

149
00:10:11,742 --> 00:10:13,828
Who's got pretty feathers?

150
00:10:14,662 --> 00:10:15,704
( SQUAWKING )

151
00:10:15,913 --> 00:10:17,123
( GASPS )

152
00:10:19,416 --> 00:10:20,668
( SCREECHES )

153
00:10:20,751 --> 00:10:22,711
You're right, Hawky. This is bad.

154
00:10:37,852 --> 00:10:41,689
Toph, when I was in town, I found
something that you're not gonna like.

155
00:10:42,148 --> 00:10:44,316
Well, it sounds like a sheet of paper,

156
00:10:44,400 --> 00:10:46,819
but I guess you're referring to
what's on the sheet of paper.

157
00:10:47,528 --> 00:10:49,864
It's a wanted poster, of you.

158
00:10:50,197 --> 00:10:51,866
They've nicknamed you "the runaway."

159
00:10:52,366 --> 00:10:54,869
A wanted poster! That's so great.

160
00:10:55,578 --> 00:10:56,704
"The runaway."

161
00:10:56,787 --> 00:10:58,164
I love my new nickname.

162
00:10:58,247 --> 00:10:59,957
Is there a picture of me?
Does it look good?

163
00:11:03,878 --> 00:11:05,671
Well, yeah, actually,
it does look pretty good.

164
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:07,464
But, Toph, you're missing the point.

165
00:11:08,048 --> 00:11:09,341
Maybe Katara was right.

166
00:11:09,550 --> 00:11:11,552
These scams are drawing
too much attention to us.

167
00:11:12,094 --> 00:11:14,096
Don't be such a worrywart
like your sister.

168
00:11:14,430 --> 00:11:15,556
Think of it this way.

169
00:11:15,639 --> 00:11:18,184
Now you have plenty of money
to help with the invasion plan.

170
00:11:19,476 --> 00:11:20,936
Well, that is true.

171
00:11:21,395 --> 00:11:23,772
I had this idea of making armor for Appa.

172
00:11:24,190 --> 00:11:25,524
( GRUMBLES )

173
00:11:26,358 --> 00:11:29,862
Here's a little extra so you can get
yourself a nice map of the Fire Nation.

174
00:11:30,154 --> 00:11:31,197
You know what?

175
00:11:31,322 --> 00:11:32,489
Make it an atlas.

176
00:11:32,698 --> 00:11:35,284
I do like expensive atlases...

177
00:11:35,492 --> 00:11:39,038
Of course you do, and that's why
this wanted poster

178
00:11:39,121 --> 00:11:41,457
is going to stay our little secret.

179
00:11:45,377 --> 00:11:48,214
Sokka, tell me you didn't buy a bird.

180
00:11:48,797 --> 00:11:51,342
Not just a bird. A messenger bird.

181
00:11:51,425 --> 00:11:54,595
Now we can send messages
all over the world, even to Gran-gran.

182
00:11:55,054 --> 00:11:56,639
Wow, how does it work?

183
00:11:57,473 --> 00:12:00,517
Hmm, uh, I never actually
thought about that.

184
00:12:00,809 --> 00:12:03,771
Hawky, Gran-gran, South Pole.

185
00:12:04,355 --> 00:12:05,564
( SQUAWKS )

186
00:12:05,648 --> 00:12:06,774
I think he gets it.

187
00:12:06,982 --> 00:12:08,275
( SCREECHING )

188
00:12:09,109 --> 00:12:11,195
Hawky, make nice!

189
00:12:11,403 --> 00:12:12,738
Bad Hawky.

190
00:12:19,954 --> 00:12:22,373
Well, look who decided to join us.

191
00:12:22,456 --> 00:12:23,749
Where have you two been?

192
00:12:23,832 --> 00:12:25,251
Off scamming again?

193
00:12:25,709 --> 00:12:26,919
Yes, we were.

194
00:12:27,419 --> 00:12:30,756
And I suppose you don't think
what you're doing is dangerous at all?

195
00:12:31,006 --> 00:12:32,007
No, I don't.

196
00:12:32,091 --> 00:12:33,133
Really?

197
00:12:33,217 --> 00:12:34,510
Yes, really.

198
00:12:34,593 --> 00:12:37,012
Well then, what's this?

199
00:12:37,596 --> 00:12:39,014
I don't know!

200
00:12:39,098 --> 00:12:41,183
I mean, seriously, what's with you people?

201
00:12:41,267 --> 00:12:42,434
I'm blind!

202
00:12:42,768 --> 00:12:44,186
It's a wanted poster of you.

203
00:12:44,270 --> 00:12:45,562
"The runaway."

204
00:12:45,771 --> 00:12:48,524
Is that what you're called now?
Are you proud of this?

205
00:12:48,691 --> 00:12:49,692
Where did you get that?

206
00:12:49,775 --> 00:12:51,568
It doesn't matter where I got it.
The fact is...

207
00:12:51,652 --> 00:12:52,945
You went through my stuff.

208
00:12:53,028 --> 00:12:54,280
You had no right.

209
00:12:54,738 --> 00:12:57,074
Your stuff was messy,
and I was just straightening up,

210
00:12:57,157 --> 00:12:58,742
and I happened to stumble across it.

211
00:12:59,159 --> 00:13:01,829
That's a lie. You're lying, Katara.

212
00:13:02,413 --> 00:13:06,542
Fine, it's a lie, but you've been
so out of control lately,

213
00:13:06,625 --> 00:13:08,043
I knew something was up.

214
00:13:08,210 --> 00:13:10,546
I knew you were hiding something,
and you were.

215
00:13:11,088 --> 00:13:13,841
Don't you walk away from me
while I'm talking to you.

216
00:13:14,174 --> 00:13:15,217
Oh, really, mom?

217
00:13:15,467 --> 00:13:16,552
Or what are you going to do?

218
00:13:16,635 --> 00:13:17,636
Send me to my room?

219
00:13:17,761 --> 00:13:18,846
I wish I could.

220
00:13:18,929 --> 00:13:22,516
Well, you can't, because you're not my mom
and you're not their mom.

221
00:13:23,642 --> 00:13:24,935
I never said I was.

222
00:13:25,185 --> 00:13:27,062
No, but you certainly act like it.

223
00:13:27,354 --> 00:13:30,274
You think it's your job
to boss everyone around, but it's not.

224
00:13:30,482 --> 00:13:32,943
You're just a regular kid
like the rest of us,

225
00:13:33,027 --> 00:13:35,362
so stop acting like you
can tell me what to do.

226
00:13:35,487 --> 00:13:37,281
I can do whatever I want.

227
00:13:39,116 --> 00:13:40,701
I don't act that way.

228
00:13:41,035 --> 00:13:43,120
Sokka, do I act motherly?

229
00:13:43,329 --> 00:13:44,955
Hey, I'm staying out of this one.

230
00:13:45,414 --> 00:13:46,415
What do you think, Aang?

231
00:13:46,498 --> 00:13:47,708
Do I act like a mom?

232
00:13:47,791 --> 00:13:49,418
Well, I...

233
00:13:49,501 --> 00:13:50,961
Stop rubbing your eye
and speak clearly when you talk.

234
00:13:51,045 --> 00:13:52,296
Yes, ma'am.

235
00:13:52,546 --> 00:13:54,423
I can't be around you right now.

236
00:13:54,631 --> 00:13:56,842
Well, I can't be around you.

237
00:13:59,303 --> 00:14:00,846
-( SQUAWKS )
- I know, Hawky.

238
00:14:01,055 --> 00:14:02,389
Why can't they just get along?

239
00:14:07,144 --> 00:14:10,481
Hey, Aang, you want to test out
my messenger hawk with me?

240
00:14:10,647 --> 00:14:11,648
I've got an idea.

241
00:14:11,732 --> 00:14:12,733
Sure.

242
00:14:13,317 --> 00:14:18,113
I'm gonna send a note to Katara and say
it's from Toph, who wants to apologize.

243
00:14:18,322 --> 00:14:20,407
Then everyone will be friends again.

244
00:14:20,616 --> 00:14:24,161
I got to say, Sokka, you continue
to impress me with your ideas.

245
00:14:24,370 --> 00:14:25,621
Eh, it's a gift.

246
00:14:28,582 --> 00:14:30,000
"Dear Katara.

247
00:14:30,209 --> 00:14:32,336
"Sorry for everything.

248
00:14:32,419 --> 00:14:33,754
"Your friend, Toph."

249
00:14:41,011 --> 00:14:42,096
( SQUAWKING )

250
00:14:46,058 --> 00:14:47,935
I know this is from you, Sokka.

251
00:14:48,018 --> 00:14:49,937
Toph can't write.

252
00:14:50,020 --> 00:14:52,481
Ugh! You're all driving me crazy.

253
00:14:53,941 --> 00:14:55,818
I can't believe
we forgot Toph can't write.

254
00:14:56,026 --> 00:14:57,528
Yep, we're idiots.

255
00:14:58,237 --> 00:15:01,448
I guess Plan B is we send a note to Toph
pretending it's from Katara.

256
00:15:01,824 --> 00:15:03,909
I think we're gonna run into
a similar problem...

257
00:15:03,992 --> 00:15:06,036
-( SQUAWKS )
- Sorry, Hawky.

258
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:07,996
Looks like I'm gonna have
to do this without your help.

259
00:15:09,790 --> 00:15:11,375
Come on, we need to talk.

260
00:15:20,843 --> 00:15:22,344
TOPH: So, let me guess.

261
00:15:22,428 --> 00:15:23,929
You brought me out here
to tell me your sister's

262
00:15:24,012 --> 00:15:26,515
not as annoying as I make her out to be.

263
00:15:26,598 --> 00:15:28,183
Nah, she's pretty much a pain.

264
00:15:29,643 --> 00:15:31,812
She's always got to be right
about everything,

265
00:15:31,895 --> 00:15:34,857
and she gets all bossy,
and involved, and in your business.

266
00:15:35,190 --> 00:15:37,359
TOPH: Yeah, I don't know
how you can deal with it.

267
00:15:38,026 --> 00:15:40,612
SOKKA: Actually, in a way, I rely on it.

268
00:15:41,321 --> 00:15:42,531
TOPH: I don't understand.

269
00:15:42,781 --> 00:15:45,451
When our mom died,
that was the hardest time in my life.

270
00:15:45,826 --> 00:15:50,497
Our family was a mess, but Katara,
she had so much strength.

271
00:15:50,706 --> 00:15:53,834
She stepped up
and took on so much responsibility.

272
00:15:54,042 --> 00:15:56,587
She helped fill the void
that was left by our mom.

273
00:15:56,795 --> 00:15:58,964
I guess I never thought about that.

274
00:15:59,506 --> 00:16:01,216
I'm gonna tell you something crazy.

275
00:16:01,425 --> 00:16:03,343
I never told anyone this before...

276
00:16:03,427 --> 00:16:07,514
But honestly, I'm not sure I can remember
what my mother looked like.

277
00:16:08,015 --> 00:16:11,977
It really seems like, my whole life,
Katara's been the one looking out for me.

278
00:16:12,561 --> 00:16:16,106
She's always been the one that's there,
and now...

279
00:16:16,315 --> 00:16:20,944
When I try to remember my mom,
Katara's is the only face I can picture.

280
00:16:21,570 --> 00:16:25,199
TOPH: The truth is,
sometimes Katara does act motherly,

281
00:16:25,449 --> 00:16:27,159
but that's not always a bad thing.

282
00:16:27,576 --> 00:16:30,787
She's compassionate and kind,
and she actually cares about me.

283
00:16:31,497 --> 00:16:33,957
You know, the real me.

284
00:16:34,875 --> 00:16:36,793
That's more than my own mom.

285
00:16:39,046 --> 00:16:41,215
Don't ever tell her I said any of this.

286
00:16:41,548 --> 00:16:43,008
Hey, my lips are sealed.

287
00:16:46,929 --> 00:16:48,555
( PURRING )

288
00:16:51,517 --> 00:16:53,519
Hi, Toph. Um, I want to...

289
00:16:53,602 --> 00:16:54,770
Katara, stop.

290
00:16:54,978 --> 00:16:56,021
You don't need to apologize.

291
00:16:56,104 --> 00:16:58,023
I was the one being stupid.

292
00:16:58,106 --> 00:17:01,026
These scams are out of control,
and I'm done with them.

293
00:17:01,527 --> 00:17:03,862
Actually, I wasn't going to apologize.

294
00:17:04,530 --> 00:17:07,199
I was gonna say,
I want to pull a scam with you.

295
00:17:08,492 --> 00:17:10,494
What? You want to pull a scam?

296
00:17:10,911 --> 00:17:13,914
Not just any scam. The ultimate scam.

297
00:17:14,164 --> 00:17:16,708
What do you say, Toph? Just me and you.

298
00:17:16,917 --> 00:17:18,168
One last go.

299
00:17:18,377 --> 00:17:19,419
You in?

300
00:17:19,503 --> 00:17:20,921
You know I'm in.

301
00:17:21,129 --> 00:17:23,090
Now what's this idea of yours?

302
00:17:23,173 --> 00:17:24,174
( BOTH GROANING )

303
00:17:28,428 --> 00:17:29,638
The plan is simple.

304
00:17:29,721 --> 00:17:32,307
This wanted poster says
you're worth a lot of money,

305
00:17:32,391 --> 00:17:34,935
ten times more than you've made
in all your scams...

306
00:17:35,519 --> 00:17:38,397
So, I'm gonna turn you in
and collect the reward.

307
00:17:38,480 --> 00:17:41,650
Then you metalbend yourself out of jail,
and we're on our way.

308
00:17:41,817 --> 00:17:43,068
( PANTING )

309
00:17:43,151 --> 00:17:44,861
( GRUNTING )

310
00:17:46,280 --> 00:17:48,031
How could you do this to me?

311
00:17:48,323 --> 00:17:49,700
You betrayed me!

312
00:17:50,534 --> 00:17:52,244
You brought this on yourself.

313
00:17:52,578 --> 00:17:53,745
I had no choice.

314
00:18:00,252 --> 00:18:03,338
You did the right thing
by turning in the runaway.

315
00:18:03,422 --> 00:18:05,507
The right thing is its own reward.

316
00:18:05,632 --> 00:18:07,676
Well, I'm happy to hear you say that.

317
00:18:08,802 --> 00:18:11,388
But... I still want the actual reward.

318
00:18:11,722 --> 00:18:13,140
Of course. Right this way.

319
00:18:28,030 --> 00:18:30,032
Hey, what kind of cell is this?

320
00:18:30,574 --> 00:18:31,742
A wooden one.

321
00:18:40,959 --> 00:18:43,754
That's her. That's the girl
you were looking for.

322
00:18:53,347 --> 00:18:56,183
Do you think this scam of theirs
should be taking this long?

323
00:18:56,266 --> 00:18:58,018
I was just wondering the same thing.

324
00:18:58,101 --> 00:18:59,144
We'd better check it out.

325
00:18:59,227 --> 00:19:01,188
-( SQUAWKING )
- You two behave.

326
00:19:01,271 --> 00:19:02,898
Appa's in charge.

327
00:19:03,565 --> 00:19:04,691
( GRUMBLES )

328
00:19:07,110 --> 00:19:08,654
( BOTH SCREECHING )

329
00:19:08,737 --> 00:19:10,781
( ROARS )

330
00:19:13,950 --> 00:19:15,285
Wait, it's a trap.

331
00:19:15,661 --> 00:19:17,871
Really? No kidding.

332
00:19:18,246 --> 00:19:20,874
Is that why we're sitting
in a wooden cage right now?

333
00:19:21,208 --> 00:19:23,460
Gee, how'd you figure out it was a trap?

334
00:19:23,627 --> 00:19:25,128
Not for us, Katara.

335
00:19:25,337 --> 00:19:26,588
We're the bait.

336
00:19:26,797 --> 00:19:28,173
He wants Aang.

337
00:19:28,298 --> 00:19:29,549
Oh...

338
00:19:29,633 --> 00:19:31,301
I can't believe I was so stupid.

339
00:19:31,802 --> 00:19:34,388
See, this is exactly why
I'm against these scams.

340
00:19:34,471 --> 00:19:35,889
I knew this would happen.

341
00:19:36,014 --> 00:19:38,141
But this was your idea.

342
00:19:38,225 --> 00:19:39,434
I know.

343
00:19:39,851 --> 00:19:42,521
I wanted to show you
that I'm not so motherly.

344
00:19:42,729 --> 00:19:45,607
I wanted to show you
that I can have fun, too.

345
00:19:45,982 --> 00:19:47,943
Katara, you are fun.

346
00:19:48,485 --> 00:19:51,071
If nothing else,
you're at least fun to argue with.

347
00:19:51,655 --> 00:19:54,825
I know your relationship
with your parents is complicated,

348
00:19:55,325 --> 00:19:57,035
and I shouldn't have said what I said.

349
00:19:57,244 --> 00:19:58,245
It's okay.

350
00:19:58,704 --> 00:20:03,041
I was really mad when you said that
because, well, because maybe it's true.

351
00:20:03,333 --> 00:20:08,088
I try not to think about it, but when
I left, I probably really hurt them.

352
00:20:08,755 --> 00:20:10,173
( SNIFFLES )

353
00:20:11,675 --> 00:20:13,343
Where do you think they might be?

354
00:20:13,427 --> 00:20:15,011
Where do you think anyone is?

355
00:20:23,729 --> 00:20:25,063
( INHALES DEEPLY )

356
00:20:28,442 --> 00:20:29,609
Sokka, watch out!

357
00:20:29,693 --> 00:20:30,736
( YELLING )

358
00:20:31,027 --> 00:20:33,530
It's sparky-sparky boom man.

359
00:20:33,697 --> 00:20:36,283
You know, I'm starting to think
that name doesn't quite fit.

360
00:20:42,748 --> 00:20:44,374
( BOTH SCREAM )

361
00:20:46,042 --> 00:20:48,044
-( STRAINING )
- What are we gonna do?

362
00:20:48,128 --> 00:20:50,172
I don't know.
I wish we had some earth or water.

363
00:20:50,255 --> 00:20:51,256
We need bendables.

364
00:20:51,965 --> 00:20:53,216
What about your meteor bracelet?

365
00:20:53,383 --> 00:20:54,384
You could make a saw.

366
00:20:54,801 --> 00:20:56,303
I left it back at camp.

367
00:20:56,386 --> 00:20:58,221
I was worried they would take it.

368
00:20:59,181 --> 00:21:00,390
( SIGHS )

369
00:21:08,523 --> 00:21:10,317
Um, Katara?

370
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,443
Are you okay?

371
00:21:11,777 --> 00:21:12,778
Just fine.

372
00:21:12,903 --> 00:21:14,446
Well, what are you doing?

373
00:21:14,529 --> 00:21:16,740
I'm making my own water.

374
00:21:23,330 --> 00:21:25,415
Katara, you're a genius.

375
00:21:25,499 --> 00:21:27,918
A sweaty, stinky genius.

376
00:21:36,802 --> 00:21:38,428
( GRUNTING )

377
00:21:41,473 --> 00:21:42,808
This guy is too good.

378
00:21:42,891 --> 00:21:44,893
He shoots fire from his brain.

379
00:21:45,227 --> 00:21:47,312
We should split up.
He can't chase us both.

380
00:21:59,449 --> 00:22:01,451
( SCREAMING )

381
00:22:04,496 --> 00:22:05,539
( GRUNTS )

382
00:22:14,714 --> 00:22:15,966
Aang, get up.

383
00:22:17,551 --> 00:22:18,635
TOPH: Let's get out of here.

384
00:22:22,097 --> 00:22:23,306
( GRUNTING )

385
00:22:31,982 --> 00:22:33,608
( GROANING )

386
00:22:35,193 --> 00:22:36,236
( GROWLING )

387
00:22:40,740 --> 00:22:42,158
( GRUNTS )

388
00:22:48,248 --> 00:22:49,374
Hey, I got it.

389
00:22:49,457 --> 00:22:51,042
The perfect name for that guy.

390
00:22:51,126 --> 00:22:52,168
Combustion Man.

391
00:22:52,252 --> 00:22:53,253
Good job, Sokka.

392
00:22:53,336 --> 00:22:55,922
Now let's get out of here
before Combustion Man catches us.

393
00:22:56,423 --> 00:22:58,049
SOKKA: See? It fits so well.

394
00:23:02,721 --> 00:23:04,764
APPA: ( GROWLING )

395
00:23:05,807 --> 00:23:07,267
Well, I'm exhausted.

396
00:23:07,517 --> 00:23:08,894
Hawky, how about you, buddy?

397
00:23:09,060 --> 00:23:11,855
Yeah, you're such a lazy little bird.

398
00:23:12,355 --> 00:23:14,858
Katara, I need your help.

399
00:23:17,235 --> 00:23:18,612
What is it, Toph?

400
00:23:18,695 --> 00:23:20,780
I need you to write
some things down for me.

401
00:23:21,114 --> 00:23:22,991
I want to send a letter to my parents.

402
00:23:24,701 --> 00:23:26,453
I'll be happy to help.

403
00:23:38,715 --> 00:23:40,258
SOKKA: Hey, where'd Hawky go?

404
00:23:48,850 --> 00:23:50,852
( CLOSING THEME PLAYING )
